// A lineage that runs only through negation (BENCH-137; the property of Molly's negative_support_test, R10 T14 and
// R06 D26), written for this corpus. The server s acknowledges the client c's request once; c's outcome is good unless
// the acknowledgement is overdue. The outcome's positive lineage is c's own request, which no fault can remove; the
// acknowledgement reaches it only through `notin overdue`. A search without negative support (TEST-025 Off) has no
// hypothesis and reports no counterexample; conservative negative support (CR-31) finds the lost acknowledgement.
// Every rule is an ordinary deductive, `@next` or `@async` rule (no absolute-time body atom). Blossom golden corpus,
// re-derived (derived = true); see ../../README.md.

ack(C, S)@async :- asked(S, C);
ack(C, S)@next :- ack(C, S);
request(C, S)@next :- request(C, S);
overdue(C, S) :- request(C, S), notin ack(C, S);

// spec: pre holds once c has asked; post also needs the acknowledgement not to be overdue
pre(C, S) :- request(C, S);
post(C, S) :- request(C, S), notin overdue(C, S);

request("c", "s")@1;
asked("s", "c")@1;
